@startuml 21-tutorial-journey
!include _style.puml
title Tutorial journey: from empty machine to a returned order
|Setup|
start
:1. ./start.sh\n(Postgres x3, Temporal, Keycloak);
:2. Start CRM (Temporal enabled);
:3. Start ERP (--temporal.enabled=true);
:4. Start OrchestrationWorker;
:5. Seed ERP products + inventory (SQL);
|Customer|
:6. POST /customers;
:7. Watch CustomerOnboarding in Temporal UI;
:8. GET /customers/{id}/integration -> Active;
|Sales|
:9. Create opportunity;
:10. Create quote with lines;
:11. Submit (and approve as a different admin);
:12. Accept;
:13. Watch QuoteToOrder; quote -> Ordered;
|Failure drills|
:14. Out of stock, price below floor, worker down;
|Returns|
:15. POST /quotes/{id}/returns;
:16. Send goodsReceived signal;
:17. Check stock restored; return Completed;
|Operate|
:18. Reconcile, audit trail, outbox queries;
stop
@enduml
